From 114ced67cfc7be87e225e0c207dc75eedb073919 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SEGURIDAD-PORTES-33 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 09:49:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] v8: load dynamic JS parameter count in builtin prolog
 (c20e1a6e22, crbug 581560002)

Port of the V8 15.9 merge c20e1a6e22 ([M159] [sandbox] Load dynamic JS
parameter count in builtin prolog; main 30ec9a07; bugs 465487205,
581560002) to 15.6.75.66 as patches/v8. TFJ trampoline builtins now
load and cache the dynamic parameter count from the JSDispatchTable at
the very start of the prolog, before a stack check or allocation can
trigger a GC that frees the unrooted incoming dispatch entry.

All code hunks apply unchanged to 15.6.75.66. mjsunit.status takes the
new SKIP in the 15.6 'not has_webassembly' block, on top of the
existing FlyWeb hunk. New test sandbox/regress/regress-581560002.js.
The code cache epoch is already 41 for this batch.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MwmK2kdhDkMC93UBtLuPkF
