+# FlyWeb: release after 3.2.2 (softmac `seguridad/siguiente-3`), V8 fix c20e1a6e22 (crbug 581560002), ported from the M159 merge
+
+SEGURIDAD-PORTES-33, 24-11-2026 (softmac `FlyWeb/seguridad/siguiente-3/brave-core/0002`). **Not merged to V8 15.6
+upstream yet**: ported from the M159 merge c20e1a6e22 (V8 15.9.128.35; cherry-pick of 30ec9a07 from main; bugs 465487205
+and 581560002). Severity not published; it is a V8 sandbox bug.
+
+- TFJ trampoline builtins read the dynamic JS parameter count from the JSDispatchTable entry of the incoming dispatch
+  handle late, after `PerformStackCheck` or a call/allocation. A GC there could free the unrooted entry, and the count was
+  then read from a freed (and possibly reused) entry. Now `EmitBuiltinProlog` loads and caches the count at the very
+  start; `SetSupportsDynamicParameterCount` and `JSTrampolineAssembler::CompileLazy` take the cached value, Torque passes
+  it instead of the `DispatchHandle` type, and the load sites `DCHECK(IsAtStart())`.
+- Every code hunk applies unchanged to 15.6.75.66 (18 files); no other `patches/v8` file touches them. All 15.6 callers of
+  the changed signatures (`SetSupportsDynamicParameterCount` in `base.tq`, `js-to-wasm.tq` x3,
+  `wasm-interpreter-wrappers.tq`; `CompileLazy` in `js-trampoline-assembler.*`; `GetDispatchHandleType` and
+  `DISPATCH_HANDLE_TYPE_STRING` in Torque) are in the patched files. `mjsunit.status`: the new `[SKIP]` goes into the 15.6
+  `not has_webassembly` block, on top of the existing FlyWeb hunk. Plus the test `sandbox/regress/regress-581560002.js`.
+
+**Cache epoch:** covered by the single 40 -> 41 bump of `siguiente-3` (`brave-core/0001`).
+
+To check (D8-LINUX): build `v8` (Torque and the builtins change), `d8` with the sandbox testing flags, mjsunit
+`sandbox/regress/regress-581560002`, `wasm/*` and `sandbox/*`.
+
